+          <h2 id="future-heading">AI can write the code.<br>Who checks the code?</h2>
+        </div>
+        <span class="future-tag">Proceed with curiosity</span>
+      </div>
+      <p class="future-intro">Across our very scientific sample of five, we agree: AI is already a brilliant accelerator for boilerplate, tests, and turning ideas into working software. It can also miss context, invent a confident bug, or leave a security hole wearing a tiny disguise.</p>
+      <div class="principles">
+        <div class="principle"><strong>Today: pair, don't autopilot</strong><span>Use AI to move faster on repetitive work. Keep a human reviewing logic, tests, and security.</span></div>
+        <div class="principle"><strong>Tomorrow: design &amp; audit</strong><span>Less time on raw syntax; more on architecture, system constraints, and proving things work.</span></div>
+        <div class="principle"><strong>Always: stay responsible</strong><span>Generated code is a draft, not a hall pass. The engineer still owns what ships.</span></div>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+
+  <footer class="page-shell signoff">
+    <span><strong>Five people. One shared suspicion of “it works on my machine.”</strong></span>
+    <span>Built by an agent, supervised by humans.</span>
+  </footer>
+
+  <script>
+    const themeButton = document.querySelector("#theme-toggle");
+    const themeLabel = document.querySelector("#theme-label");
+    const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
+    const initialTheme = savedTheme === "black" ? "black" : "night";
+
+    function setTheme(theme) {
+      document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
+      const isBlack = theme === "black";
+      themeLabel.textContent = isBlack ? "Black mode" : "Night mode";
+      themeButton.setAttribute("aria-label", `Switch to ${isBlack ? "night" : "black"} theme`);
+      themeButton.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(isBlack));
+      localStorage.setItem("upb-theme", theme);
+    }
+
+    setTheme(initialTheme);
+    themeButton.addEventListener("click", () => {
+      setTheme(document.documentElement.dataset.theme === "night" ? "black" : "night");
+    });
+  </script>
+</body>
